 "rows": {
  "tar:entrapment-hediff": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "amazing defensibility of difficult areas, to be used by deep desert tribes and other primitives",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v1",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:sinking-render": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Test of our ability to make meaningful animation. We should spend some good time on this to really demo what we know how to do, or perhaps study other mods that make custom animations to inspire ourselves.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:stratified-dig-sites": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "This is pure gold. Fossils, dead bodies with inventory stuck on them, each one a piece of a story from the past that goes more ancient as you dig. But the digging gets slower and harder as you go. Would perhaps need to install a pump that removes the tar elsewhere on the map to enable the digging at all, while it continues to ooze in from deep sources below.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:canal-flow-engineering": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "This is a general new mechanic that we can use in many places. Dig channels that flood with water, ooze, slime, oil, tar, propane fuel... let's explore this deeply. Could be amazing realism. I'm inspired! This allows bases to dig trenches and flood them as a real defense. Will pay off in many more scenarios. This isn't Utinni or even Star Wars scope, this is general RimMaster level awesomeness mod.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:flood-and-ignite": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Not kill outright, just burns like normal fire. But yes, toxic thick smoke that obscures and produces coughing and stinging eyes and stink.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:tar-moats": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "nope, this is in! Pawns with goals inside a region make the call to go across it, while if there's any way around it they do so.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "dream",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:tar-creatures": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Very star wars to reveal that a tar pit harbors a huge creature that not only thrives in tar but actually excretes it as a biological outcome. If captured, continues to do so at a very slow rate (not magical, very slow). However, even pits without one of these creatures still fill trenches and such from the tar sources deep underground.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "dream",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:geyser-incident": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Superb vile shock. Add creatures that consume tar too and run towards these events/moments. Able to mode through the tar easily unlike trapped creatures. They may like to eat tar-encrusted pawns too.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v1",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:pit-wakes-setpiece": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Totally! The things in ancient dangers are the source, but also egg forms of creatures that hatch when disturbed (tar beasts), as well as things people maliciously put down there (grenades/bombs). Especially if it's in the territory of a terrible faction that's vindictive against territory thieves.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "dream",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "tar:chemfuel-economy": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Yes, but it's slow and gross. Tar oozes out of the pipe joints. Only slowly produces chemfuel.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "tar_pits_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:lake": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "And exotic creatures within the lake. Could even be a wild underwater adventure WITHIN a propane lake (like the ocean biome we're building, but with stranger contents... and the ship must carefully lower itself into FUEL rather than water this time)",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v1",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:vents": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Puffing gas sometimes self-ignites, but doesn't deplete until the player starts actively pumping it out. That explains why the natural ones are even still there when the player arrives. removing the pumping apparatus should trigger a violent release map-wide that's very dangerously flammable until it clears by the wind.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v1",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:pipe-rupture": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "There should be some valves that can be accessed to manually shut the pipe down on the map, or else the player just \"leaves it that way\" and wonders what happens. Huge negative faction relationship from this. (or positive if it was your mission to do so)",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:saturation": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Absolutely! During the massive gas release event it should be a transient condition. But there should be caverns where this is just perpetually true (a common occurrance on Earth in mines anyway). Also true witin the \"dead sarlacc\" type dungeons, along with rotstink gas.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v1",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:tanker-economy": {
   "d": "cut",
   "n": "You're not extra flammable on the way home, just right next to that explosive lake... and you have to run long flexible pipes from your ship to the lake, because of your thrusters.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:lake-creature": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Of course it might! Not guaranteed, but often. And it should be seen moving around the lake as a submerged V-shaped wake trailing around, just to add suspense. If it sees the pawns/pipe, it approaches and attacks. But the loud pumping agitates them and makes them start to look around more swiftly. NOT the reason the propane lake is there, they just dwell within it.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "v2",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:tar-interplay": {
   "d": "cut",
   "n": "too much, no need",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "dream",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
  "gas:saturation-heist": {
   "d": "v1",
   "n": "Give them better weapons. Sonic from the genosians, for example. Or primitive javelains and catapults. Strictly non-flammable, non-temperature-based, non explosives. Vibro-weaponry.",
   "touched": true,
   "prefill": "dream",
   "doc": "propane_gas_deep_design.md"
  },
